recursive probability density estimators of stationary processes\n\nAuthor links open overlay panel Elias Masry ^{∗}, László Györfi\n\n\nView PDFDownload full issue\n\nCite\n\nAdd to Mendeley\n\nShare\n\n10.1016/0047-259X(87)90077-7\n\n## Abstract\n\nLet {X_{j}}_{j = − ∞}^{∞} be a vector-valued stationary process with a first-order univariate probability density f on R^{d}. We consider the recursive estimation of f(x) from n observations {X_{j}}_{j=1}^{n} which need not be independent. For processes {X_{j}}_{j = − ∞}^{∞} which are asymptotically uncorrelated, we establish sharp rates for the almost sure convergence of kernel-type estimators f_{n}(x).\n\n## MSC\n\n62G05\n\n;\n\n62M09\n\n## Keywords\n\nrecursive probability density estimation\n\n;\n\nweakly dependent stationary processes\n\n;\n\nalmost sure convergence rates\n\nView PDF\n\n^{∗}\n    \n\nThe work of E. Masry was supported by the Office of Naval Research under contract N00014-84-L-0042.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nComputational Science Center - Otmar Scherzer (https://csc.univie.ac.at/scherzer/)\nciteturn994search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Scherzer Tikhonov type regularization methods: history and recent progress In P. ... @incollection{LenSch04, author = {Lenzen, F. and Scherzer, O.}, title = {{T}ikhonov type regularization methods: history and recent progress}, booktitle = {Proceedings of ECCOMAS 2004}, editor = {Neittaanm{\\\"a}ki, P. and Rossi, T. and Majava, K. and Pironneau, O.}, location = {Jyv{\\\"a}skyl{\\\"a}, Finland}, publisher = {University of Jyv{\\\"a}skyl{\\\"a}}, year = {2004}, }\nFunded by the Austrian Science Fund (FWF) within the FSP S105 - \"Photoacoustic Imaging\"\n\n(author's post print; this is the peer reviewed version of the following article: Causality analysis of frequency-dependent wave attenuation Mathematical Methods in the Applied Sciences, 34:108–124, which has been published in final form at 10.1002/mma.